I spent my twentieth birthday with Tucker.
It was a rare sunny day in the Mistwoods, and we met up at <style=Hint_BgD>our old spot</style>.
Tucker always liked burying himself there, and no one but me could ever call him out.
We had agreed long in advance that we’d celebrate together today.
Everyone in the Mistwoods, feel the power of our “Magic Sound Duet”!
...
The Witchins who had gathered for a music party all covered their ears and ran off.
Our magic sound is more powerful than theirs, hands down!
...
Even the Pomeggs, who love a good bit of noise, ran off.
...
Looking around, there wasn’t a single Hummin left.
...
Sure enough, we made everyone in the Mistwoods hear our singing!
Although no one could tell we were singing the “Birthday Song.”
...
I never used to like singing the birthday song, nor celebrating birthdays.
Because I’ve been off-key since I was little, and everyone always laughed at me.
But singing together with Tucker, even if the whole Mistwoods can’t stand it, I’m happy.
I’m starting to look forward to my next birthday.
The next birthday, and the one after, and the one after that... I want to spend them all with Tucker!Thank you! You’re a good Susuta!You don’t have enough training coinsAn irresistibly cute photo of a Fentuft. One look is enough to melt your heart.A world-weary Inferlupa tells you: come back during the day if you want a real fight. At night, the old-timers have nothing left to give. Still, if you insist, they’ll humor you.Server ProgressYoung people have so many ideas. I could never come up with as many perfume concepts as Sunia...
No wonder Lady Irelia favors her the most.This exhibition is amazing! I got a whole bag full of material for my paper!Sunshade Water LilyThese curious energy flows... Glimmer Trees... I wonder where they end...45<color=#5090df>%s</color> tossed fruit peel on <color=#5090df>%s’s</color> head, which led to a huge fight that ends with <color=#5090df>%s</color> being beaten up.Vertical beige paneling lines the inside, while the outside has a smooth greige finish. A sturdy brick-and-stone base anchors the low wall, and its warm, understated palette feels simple without looking plain.Dance among the flowers, and every step carries their scent.Glynsera and Scorchhowl are both born for battle. Each leads its own kind in the fight for Beast Fang Ridge, and even Boneskies and Emberpups cannot stay out of it. During one battle, a Bonesky tumbled down a hillside and broke its leg. An Emberpup carried it back to safety. The Bonesky couldn’t understand why its enemy had saved it. The Emberpup simply said, "You’re going to be my rival one day. I can’t have you ending up as a crippled wolf, forgotten in some corner." The Emberpup’s honesty and fighting spirit inspired the Bonesky, and the two made a promise: each would become the strongest of their own kind before meeting again for a final duel. Determined to become the strongest on Beast Fang Ridge, they each set off to find their own path to strength. You became the witness to that promise. In time, the Bonesky fulfilled that promise and became Recas, the mightiest Glynsera. The leg that had once been broken became the weapon with which it claimed glory. But when the Emberpup never returned to keep its promise, loneliness slowly consumed Recas. It came to realize that the price of strength wasn’t just broken bones and battle scars, but also the cold and loneliness that came with it.Pebble PavingAuto AimNo, that’s not it! I wanted to see you myself!So why not stock up on some Aniipods?Journey DelightsBINI’s photo and my drawing match perfectly, don’t they?Insomniac CubboEnter group chat name.Woo-uh...Do you also wish to become—
