2. Quest Details:
① Pop-Up Store Check-In: Head to the entrance of the Xiaohongshu pop-up store at the northwest corner of the lower level of Horizon Square in Astra. Take a Snap there to complete the check-in Quest.
② Plant Little Sweet Potatoes: Search for "Aniimo" on Xiaohongshu to join the "Aniimo Plants Sweet Potatoes" Event and publish a related post. After approval, you can receive the "Recipe Note: Little Sweet Potato" redemption code on Xiaohongshu. Once obtained, you can plant Little Sweet Potato seeds in your Home and harvest "Captain Spud." If you grow a "Game Spud," you'll also have a chance to win cash and gold prizes on Xiaohongshu~Stardust AgateMaybe some other time!Event AnnouncementA dandelion tree growing in the Nimbus Fields.Top DecorationsTimber Serenity - Storage CabinetA plant for your Home.Holo-Battle Sim AvatarWooden StreetlampThe Journey’s EndAiryRepairingTraining Coin earnings increase by <style=Hint_BgD><customRichText(getConfigData,rogue_multi_level_talent_data,48006,param0)>%</style>.It seems the tower's master hasn't returned yet...The entrance is blocked by Tucker’s main vines... Maybe I should <style=Hint_BgD>follow the vines to find the vine cores</style>.Time Guardian StatueCan attract the following Prismana Form AniimoDefeat AlphasMalangelI have no idea what will hatch from it. Perhaps a strange new being or one I’m familiar with.Flamerions in a different color after absorbing fog as their fuel. Pretending to be glowing plants is their trick.Mutated rare wheat, sparkling with dazzling spots of light.Calm down, let me think...A frigid frost settles over your strands, accentuating your cool, sharp aura.Basic item used for catching Aniimo.Wow, you’re so talented!Stone Aniipod (Medium)Shadow ManThe Sanctum ruins scattered across Idyll were built by the Ancient Idyllians to repair damaged Veins. Descend into the depths of a Sanctum and activate long-dormant Mechina to restore the flow of Vein energy.CraftingWith nothing else to do, Hummin buries itself in the soil to absorb nutrients, looking just like a low-growing plant.After you defeat the Inferlupa, the ridgeback trees of Thousand-Fang Ridge bloom once more. The three fighters finally understand that continuing to fight in the darkest hour is what makes a true fighter, and they thank you for restoring their honor. You invite them to travel with you, but they decline, explaining that there are too many of them, and race off into the distance.Spend 1,000 Training Coins to obtain 3 random "Valor" GizmosWhen Lightning Mark detonates, it deals burst damage based on the number of stacks.Lightning MarkI’ve arrived at Driftwise Meadow, blanketed in melancholic mist.
