You’ve already completed the practical assessment, and the theory exam will review your elite training.Even after the Legendary Journey event ends, Pathfinders can still get Irisalis Petals in the following ways (except Tracing the Trail). 

1. Story
Obtain by clearing the following Story chapters: Ceremony Preparations, The Ceremony That Never Began, Colorful Fragrance, The Land of Dancing Illusions, The Land where Dreams Come True, Ancient Sacred Fragrance, Rainbow of the Ground, and A New Journey. 

2. Journey Quests
Obtain by clearing the following Journey Quests: The Legend of Mist and Light, The Legend of Echoback Landing, The Legend of Flowers and Thorns, The Legend of the Land of Falling Stars, The Legend of Thousand-Fang Ridge, The Legend of the Land of Lightning and Thunder, The Legend of Helmuts and Helgons, The Legend of the Bell of Freedom, The Legend of the Berylline Vale, and The Legend of Driftwise Meadow. 

3. Gathering
Follow Irelia’s footsteps and gather Irisalis Petals across Breezy Plains. 

4. First Alpha Clear
Get them upon your very first victory over the Breezy Plains Alpha. 

5. Elite Pathfinder Challenges
Obtain by defeating the following elite Pathfinders in Breezy Plains: Senior Wally, Senior Jilly, Senior Loulla, Senior Aster, Senior Wendell, Senior Cecelia, and Lita. 

6. Branch Nurturing
Obtain by infusing energy into the Breezy Plains Branch and unlocking its nodes. 

7. Breezy Plains Silver Badges
Obtain by claiming Silver Badges from each area in Breezy Plains. 

8. Aniimo Research
Unlock and tap the Nova Stage Aniimo Index entry inside your Aniilog, complete the research topic Collect Prismana Form, and collect them from rewards. 

9. Tracing the Trail
