- Upgrade Training Mastery will unlock more abilities.The Bolties of Blitzwood believe electricity can connect all things—even hearts. That is why they love communicating via these electric "calls", even when standing face to face. You just so happened to overhear them, and clever BINI recorded the whole conversation.While chatting with Sorora, you learn that Echoback Landing is a romantic destination formed from layers of rose-colored coral. Shy Susutas offer beautiful gifts to court potential mates, Budclaws grow grass on their heads and faithfully pair for life, and noisy Chirpis just love joining any commotion they come by. Sorora remembers nothing from before he was rescued on the shore. He became a painter by putting the hazy images from his memory onto canvas, and now travels the continent in search of clues to his past.Pathfinder, have you heard the tale of the Echobacks?C - Aniimo trainingYeah, aren’t those two families supposed to be sworn enemies?Level 40 SuppressionBefore exploring, equip a <style=Hint_BgL>backpack</style>. A good backpack lets you bring back more <style=Hint_BgL>ancient relics</style>!Bold PebblingIncreases Crit Damage against targets affected by Weakness Mark by <customRichText(calcData,buff, 2144305,param0,1,%d)>%.Alpha Tubster Transformation[Valor] No RetreatRelaxed FentuftFruit of a Starine Tree. Celestis family’s favorite food.Static Plank_Lv1Clover Tile - Almond YellowBroke Already?The Bailite strains to haul out a massive golden chest! With a loud thunk, it drops it onto the ground~
