I returned to the Mistwoods, but that old spot was gone.
Because Tucker is gone.
...
Everything has lost its color.
The noisy Hummins seem to have vanished too.
...
I stood at the maze ruins, hoping a group of Hexxins would dizzy me with their terrible songs.
But there was only silence and desolation.
...
Twenty years ago, I couldn’t wait to leave my friend and travel far away.
I wanted to escape my terrible singing.
I dreamed of having a beautiful voice.
Now, looking at this bottle of "Beautiful Voice Perfume" in my hand, I miss those days of being surrounded by awful singing more than anything.
...
I lie here and don’t want to leave.
Everything in my memory is gone. Only this place, which used to be our old spot, remains waiting for me...
