However, the brewing of the floral nectar uses seven different colored flowers.Complete any 1 type of Advanced TrainingThese Sea of Flowers dwellers have purple wings and antennae shaped like flower spikes for camouflage.Received 70 Training Coins!Level 1 Light Source Nested Transfer BuffAt the edge of a cliff, press #kPlayer/Jump#z to jump into the air. While airborne, press #kPlayer/Jump#z to enter the <style=Hint_BgL>Flying</style> state.Stone Aniipod (Large and Initially Stationary)Attack and deal <color=#d89c28>BREAK damage</color>.Invite at least 2 friends whose group chat is not yet full.Earn 8,000 Windborn StampsPlease defeat the mutated Helgon Feral!Twine with an <style=Hint_BgL>Emberpup</style>, then press <style=Hint_BgL>Skill 1</style> to use its <style=Hint_BgL>Fire Bolt</style> to burn through the obstacle.1. During the Event, Pathfinders can select a Prismana Aniimo of their choice on the Event screen. Once your Title is promoted to "Grade I Pathfinder," you can claim the selected Aniimo. You may change your selection at any time before claiming it.
2. The claimed Aniimo will be in Prismana Form, with its personality generated at random. After claiming it, the second phase, "Prismana Pact," will unlock.
3. After "Prismana Pact" is unlocked, Pathfinders can continue collecting Prismana Aniimo within the Event's designated scope. Each time a new type of Prismana Aniimo is added, the corresponding Prismana Index progress will increase.
4. If the Prismana Aniimo claimed in Phase 1 falls within the Index scope of "Prismana Pact," it will also count toward Index progress as normal. Obtaining duplicate copies of the same Prismana Aniimo will not increase progress multiple times.
5. Once Prismana Index progress reaches the specified requirements, you can claim the corresponding phase rewards.
6. Pathfinders can use "View Index" on the Event screen to check the current collection status of Prismana Aniimo and continue searching for any Prismana Aniimo not yet added.Ah yes... that's me.It seems the power of fire isn’t strong enough. Come back when you’re stronger!And I am <style=Hint_BgD>Lunara</style>, representing Lun and embodying harmony and wisdom.
