...
After leaving the Celestis outpost, I saw a very tall Starine Tree in the distance.
1. Starines
2. A high place
3. A solitary living space
All the information tells me that it must be where the Stellarys lives.
While retaining their love for Starines and high places (as members of the Celestis family), Stellaryses prefer to live alone and keep out of sight.
My following research will focus on the reason for such a peculiar trait.
...
Based on my observations, compared to Celestises, Stellaryses have significantly increased dark energy.
Combined with the information I found at the Celestis outpost, my assumption has been proven.
Stellaryses are intelligent beings to some extent. Despite the fact that they still belong to the same family as Celestises, they become, at some point, two different life forms. Aniimo are just so amazing.In the Woods Northwest of the MistwoodsDailyWanna practice climbing? Go use the pillars and walls across the way!5 Mutual FriendsThe Sea of Flowers has become more lush and beautiful in recent years, and it’s all thanks to Lady Irelia’s blessing. The quality of our aromathyst harvest has never been better!Right... I’ll probably end up taking a beating, and that might get me down for a while... but no friendship is perfect.5s after battle starts, a Pulse Crystal appears, firing a pulse every 15s after a 3s delay. Inactive while the enemy is affected by BREAK. If the pulse hits a player, it deals damage and knocks them back. Pulses can be blocked by the enemy, hitting an enemy deals <customRichText(calcData,timeline,2030101,param1,1,%d)>% BREAK damage and increases their damage taken by <customRichText(calcData,buff,4003011,param0,1,%d)>% for <customRichText(buffConfigData,4003011,duration)>s.Your Dragonsbreath Mocha has arrived, enjoy.Golden Wish paints the pale dreamscape with the color of miracles.Using a Counter Mark to deal damage has a 50% chance to instantly gain 10 EP.You’re welcome...Every <style=Hint_BgL><customRichText(calcData,buff,9126301,param0,1)></style>s, the next skill applies <style=Hint_BgL>1</style> stack of <style=Hint_BgL><link="source_8028"><u>[Drowsiness]</u></link></style> to the target.Unlocks upon completing the story [A Tale of Tide and Song]Exit spectating and go to results?Woof! Ruff!Unclaimed ChestHuge Shining SorghumA pack that can be purchased at RV level <style=Hint_BgL>3</style>.Summon the IrisalisStrange thing?Add BonusIncrease/Decrease Rank PointsYeah, that hat really suits it!Your ball?Soft, snow-white Wool that feels like a fluffy cloud to the touch.One of a kind, reject mediocrity!As for that bone... It’s the distant type. It