s needed.Twine with food-loving Celestis and complete Dr. Glass’s Trial.An extremely rare chest. There might be something nice hidden in it.Find the photographer and talk to him.Check Wolfie’s.Where did the legend of the “Perfect Racer” come from? The figure standing before the Stone Blossom may be the answer itself.-1433870634An ancient secret lies buried beneath the Mistwoods, and every flower and tree seems to guard the heart of the forest.Tell a story of the sea.Look for Blubby near ChillBeanz.Rumor: The Driftwise Meadow Research NotesFannie is calling.Omega Aniimo of the MistwoodsComplete 4 required quests in Chapter 3.Find the research notes scattered around Argent Strait.A mysterious vendor is hidden in plain sight near Horizon Square. Go check it out—you might find something unexpected!Strike the echonite at night and discover the secret of the Echoback bones.Stone Tree ClimbPlace a woodland plot in your Home.There seems to be a fanatical painter in Horizon Square of Astra...Under the gaze of countless travelers, the ruins by the roadside have stood quietly for a thousand years, untouched by wind, rain, or lightning.There seems to be some kind of magical architectureLeave the elder’s house and go to the Bloom Festival.First Sight="This is"&J67&", detailed instructions for self-modification"Mysterious chests are scattered across Idyll. They may be luggage lost by travelers, supplies left behind by Adventurers, or treasures sealed away by an ancient civilization... All of them are waiting to be discovered and opened.Vigilant EyesVein energy emerges here. Pathfinders can use Bloom for fast travel.Go visit Perfumers Avetine and Baboni.Find the legendary perfume: Perfect Mistake.Key Eco SpotPassed the quiz assessmentUpgrade RV to level 11.A cave entrance. What could be inside?Bloom: InactivePathfinders can activate Transporters, restock supplies, report your Aniimo research progress, and heal your Aniimo at the Outpost.Place a level 2 farmland plot in your Home.Upgrade RV to level 12.Storms once wore down the rocks, lightning carved the cliffs, and time gently healed them, as grass and trees softened the land’s scars.This island seems to belong to the Scar-faced Helgon, but why are there ancient murals of Infergon here? The three stone seats by the shore also seem to appear in the murals. Is it a coincidence, or are there still secrets on this island you have yet to uncover?Ram apart the stones jamming the gears and restore perfume production.Show Budclaw Under the Starry Sky.Susuta from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo at night to complete the investigation and earn points!Key Eco Spot<localizationIdTag&-2109245546>Ancient ruins divide the yellow and green earth, where the cool tones of the mountains meet the warmth of the plains.Cast [Healing Rhythm] to fully recover the Emberpup’s HP.Talk to Lita at Boomblast Arena.Answer Lita’s call.Pebbles borne by the wind have scoured the stone for ages, leaving only a patch of primal bareness. In time, they too will crack and fade, until even these marks vanish without a trace.Mysterious Chests are scattered all across Idyll. Perhaps they’re luggage left behind by travelers, supplies stashed away by adventurers, or treasures sealed away by the ancients... all waiting to be discovered and opened.Go to the Mistwoods entrance and search for the fragrance of life.The Jawling Family is known as the “Hoarding Dragon,” fond of securing and guarding treasures. As for Infergon, the Omega of the Jawling Family, what kind of treasure does it cherish?Go check on the seedling.-2031153899Dr. Glass’s research has run into trouble.Catch 1 Eko & 1 Pomegg in the Forest of Falling StarsTwine with an Emberpup!Bonesky from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!What secrets do these ancient Lumin Idols hold?D FuzzballSkippy from today’s Field Notes list can be found living near this Track point. Catch the corresponding Aniimo to complete the Field Notes and earn score rewards!Collect Bloomville’s signature outfit.Chat with the <style=Hint_BgL>scar-faced Helgon</style>.The tenacious Ignitis lies in wait within the shadows.<BR>Respawn interval: 20s (spawns at night)Proceed to Bloomville.Talk to the shrunken Scorchhowl.Use the wind field to reach the final gate.Rumor: Sword of BraveryTwo Popapuses are lost in the joy of creation. Why not go admire their work?Infergon has been guarding the Sword of Bravery, waiting for its old rival to return. By Twining with Helmut and evolving into Pawney, you are starting to uncover the legend behind the helm and the dragon.As one of Polaris Institute’s outstanding Aniimo researchers, Sayn always studies Aniimo up close in person. But luck never seems to be on his side. Through one accident after another, his precious research findings—his Aniimo research notes—have been scattered far and wide. Explore the vast continent of Idyll and help Sayn recover his research notes!Look for the one that looks like cotton candy.Look for the one with a sharp gaze.Defeat Sherro and obtain the spice.Ram the iron crate into the stone wall at the end of the track.Head to the center of the plaza.Jawling from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!A unique Aniimo nest found only in the Lost Isles. You might be able to dig up a rare <style=Hint_BgL>precious Egg</style>Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Lightning.Lightning GalePlace woodland in your Home.Dewy from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Place a Mine in your Home.Talk to #npcName#.Why is Perfumer Awen standing at the foot of the tower?Nicole, look!Go to the Dewy nest to brew an aromathyst.Into the ValleyTracking pointTwisted RootsFinish the conversation.Listen to the Bolties’ conversation.An extremely Uncommon Chest, often hiding valuable loot insideReport to Dr. Lewis.Talk to the Bulbly.Retrieve the withdrawn Hummin.Go to the Battle Art Dept. and find Lita.Budclaw from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Command your Emberpup to defeat the Celestis!Go to Echoback Landing and search for the Incense of Tolerance.Veiled TruthHelmut told you that a terrifying "dragon" has been bullying the weaker members of its kind here. Could this be the same dragon from Sorora’s story, where "a ghost raised its sword against a giant dragon"? The answer may be waiting deep in the Russet Highlands.The pattern on the stone seems to point to something.A group of Emberpups seems to be telling "ghost stories" in the dead of night?!Assemble a Bubble Gachapon in the Homebuilding Zone.Scar-faced Helgon walked over to a stone seat nearby. Is it waiting for someone to arrive?Raise your character to level 55.Talk to the nervous NimbiHelmut's Whisper IDock Lighthouse RuinsBaleetle from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!A grumpy Chirpi is fuming over a music score on the ground.Find Park Manager Ben and activate the park.Soaring GlideSub-Idyllian RuinsOn the shore of Argent Strait, a hot-tempered Chirpi is cursing at a music score that fell from the sky. But on closer inspection, it discovers that the music score is none other than “Freedom” Score by the long-lost legendary “Windgliders.” A bold idea seems to spark in the grumpy Chirpi’s mind. But can it really convince the other Chirpis?Collect scattered Lumin Amber EnergyPillar JumpFeed the Aniimo in your Home.Clue: Colorless Dream: Thousand-FangDeliver the notes found at Argent Strait to Sayn.Ore forged by ancient earthfire bathes the cavern in a crimson glow. At the end of the rock wall stand ancient ruins, as if sealing old secrets within the scorching air.Something has changed in the flower sprout at the center of the Amethyst Tree. She sleeps, and no one knows when she will awaken, but—she still seems to be doing her best to sense the world.Talk to Dr. Lewis to learn about Elite Training.Give the Lavender Cookies to Jojo.Chat with Avetine.Tall Grass AreaAsk Nova about the anomalyPass on the joy.Holo-Device MalfunctionFollow Nicole to complete your identity verification.Twine with Shelly and extinguish the flames to complete Dr. Glass’s Trial.Catch 7 different Aniimo in Nimbus FieldsThe Egg born from the Pathfinder’s prayers has appeared. Come see which Prismana Form Aniimo will hatch from it.The legend of Pawney drawing the sword to slay the dragon reappears. Although Infergon does not seem to have completely vanished, the Sword of Bravery has still brought some changes to the Helmut Family.Track Point 1Follow the Flutternym shadows to gather the next dream blossom.Answer Dr. Lewis’s callSkippy from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Burning BramblesUpgrade the RV to level 5.Place the Bud Ticket JarSend Aniimo on an outing once.A Wish from Ten Years AgoJoin the late-night chat.Chat with Johnny.A unique Aniimo nest found only on the Lost Isles. You might dig up a rare <style=Hint_BgL>Precious Egg</style>Raise your character to level 35.What’s the true meaning of happiness?Twine with a Celestis and move to the green checkpointPerfumer Avetine of Bloomville is troubled.Complete 4 required quests in Chapter 5.White flowers carpet the wilderness.Advance to Student IIICheck the hat.Upgrade the RV to level 8.Find clues in the Russet Highlands to restore the painting.To Twister PeaksRepair malfunctioning equipment in Northside, AstraUpgrade the RV to level 6.Nicole, I don’t have enough Aniipods...Find the research notes scattered around Tideblossom Coast.Hexxin from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Put in 5 large StarinesRolling ShellsSeawater has carved traces of time into the cliffs. Glory of the past has turned to dust, while the old ruins are now wrapped with an ever-expanding ant nest, silently watching over new life.Clovis hopes you can bring him Irises of six regional forms to help heal the little flower. It won’t be easy. But if Clovis’s grandfather was a seasoned flower grower, perhaps he left behind some notes with clues.Complete the initial conversation with Sayn.Warning: Alpha Aniimo<BR>Danger Level: MediumElite Challenges are open to the institute’s most promising students. Each challenge pits you against an academy-certified elite Pathfinder with an outstanding record. Passing proves your strength and earns you an exclusive institute badge and rare resources.Check the marks on the groundOutside the Celestis outpost, there’s someone who seems to be very anxious?The stone wall before the cave holds the gaze, impossible to look away.Rising WindFollow Dr. Lewis out of the OutpostClue: The Missing WindglidersBlazing WingsTalk to TysenAquatic JumpCheck the glasses.Soil and stone have buried the ancient temple, while grass and trees have covered the traces of human activity, leaving only half of a strange, jagged boulder exposed.Twine with a Hummin and blow the fruit to complete Dr. Glass’s Trial.Go back to Senior SheepyAn unhappy existence?Use fire to melt the ice and head to the next checkpointShow the collar to Leafy’s owner.Find the puzzle-loving Hummin.Electric FlowReturn and inform Jojo.Report to Senior Sheepy="This is "&J66&", edit the detailed description yourself"Give the Umbral Pickles to Jojo.Rumor: The Forest of Falling Stars Research NotesFind the bad-tempered Hummin.Investigate the strange phenomenon before youInspect the chest for cluesGive color to the Colorless Dream: Driftwise.Complete the challenge.Horizon Square is always buzzing. Wanna go see what new stock Petite’s got on the shelves?Break three mechanisms to awaken Irelia.Check: Super Truffle owned.Sell surplus wheat to the Co-op Store.Iris from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Defeat the target!At night, outside the dead forest of Beast Fang Ridge, a group of Emberpups gathers around a campfire, seemingly telling "ghost stories." What are they talking about? An Inferlupa’s head... flying through the sky?Cross the bridge and explore the residential district.Go to Horizon Square to find the painter.Shattering StoneHelmwhelp from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Skylight CameraAncient ruins stand in silence beneath ever-shifting clouds, as moss wears into broken steps and flowing water drifts with time.Catch a sleeping Aniimo {0}/3.Fragment RestorationLocated in your HomeProud and solitary, Glynsera answers only to true strength. Awaken its long-silent fighting spirit, and its honed ice blades will finally show their edge.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sUpload your catch results.A unique Aniimo nest found only on the Lost Isles. You might be able to dig up a rare <style=Hint_BgL>Precious Egg</style>Claim the reward for Elite Training Core Courses Chapter 9.Help Nicole defeat the mysterious Aniimo.Let’s light some fireworksTwine with a Bolty and make a call under the Blitz Tree.Chirpi from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Rumor: Unbroken Flameruff SpiritCheck: Has Flameheart StoneKeep talking to Fannie.Use Elemental Counters to defeat the Susuta!At Tideblossom Coast, there is a girl looking around.Pass along news of the Emberpup to a Fenrier.Under the Blitz Tree, a group of Bolties is... making phone calls?A Mementos branch store on the high street that sells Bond items.I found it!Raise your character to level 45.Give the Vine Core to SelensA special Budsquire has appeared deep within the maze.Find the legendary perfume: Heart’s Resonance.Frigid WatersGive the Super Truffle to Sunia.Discover MechanismAncient AltarBloom: Shimmering ShoreWhat secrets are hidden in this dead forest of Beast Fang Ridge? Why did the Emberpups say they had seen a flying Inferlupa head?Chasing CloudsDeliver the materialsReport to the manager of the Starwish Gacha.Head to Service Hub and browse the Seed Shop.Keep discussing festival arrangements with Jojo.Dr. Glass's Research has hit a roadblockRV Park: Echoback Landing - not activatedRumor: The Bell of FreedomFollow Nicole down.Upgrade RV to level 14.Patrol with the sparkly ShellyMysterious chests are scattered across Idyll. They may be luggage lost by travelers, supplies left behind by adventurers, or treasures sealed away by an ancient civilization... All await discovery and opening.Go to the Mistwoods and search for the scent of growth and revival.Return and speak with Dr. Lewis.Install the Aniipod Maker.Explore Tideblossom Coast and search for seafaring adventure lore.Gather the vine core in the eastern ruins.Flutternym from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo at night to complete the investigation and earn points!View orders from Astra.When a powerful Legendary Aniimo is born, Vein energy gathers in strange, unstable ways, tearing open unusual energy rifts.
