oming from the Homeland entrance.Sparki from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo at night to complete the investigation and earn points!Find Ranka.Place Harvest Gathering: Festive Lights in the Limited-Time Event Zone.A <style=Hint_BgL>talking Hummin?</style>The whitesnow rose atop Whiterose Tower.Your vision suddenly fades to black...Find and talk to Nicole.Celestis Family ResearchHelmut from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Dr. Lewis!Follow CPlace a Storage Unit in your Home.Deliver: Whitesnow Rose AromathystInto the Sea of FlowersFloral MomentShanel boutique, selling fashion for people and Aniimo.Listen to the Budsquire tell the rest of the story.Tell Bulbly a story about the sea.Upgrade a woodland plot to level 3.Go to Beast Fang Ridge and find JillyTalk to the Inferlupa.Give color to the Colorless Dream: Berylline.Talk to the trapped PomeggExplore Beast Fang Ridge to find the meaning of the Warrior.Talk to the Shulala.Rumor: What’s in the Withered Woods?Rumor: Helmut’s Secret IICollect scattered Lumin.Check the bow tie.Claim Bloomville-themed outfitsUncover the truth of "the Inferlupa’s flying head."I heard this painter is really obsessed with painting strange shapes, but very few people can make sense of them. Maybe he's waiting for the one person destined to truly appreciate his work...Set the Aniipod Maker recipe.Ask Nova what happenedHide behind the Blitz Tree at night and waitClue: Colorless Dream: DriftwiseContinue talking to Dr. LewisThis is an Alpha. Edit the detailed description as needed.Higher, faster. Dr. Glass’s Trial: Bolty!Go collect Echoback Salt from the whale bones.The ancient perfume has been crafted. Find Velouria and start looking for Irelia.Pass the Sanctum’s trial.Witness Irelia’s last dance.Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Berylline.Helgon’s island?Among the RuinsApproach and touch the Lumin Amber, then pick up all Lumin energyLately, holographic devices in Astra have been malfunctioning a lot. I’ve heard some strange things have even started appearing—what’s going on?Talk to Snowy.Fannie has delivered a fresh batch of work orders.Take a photo.Tucker is sleeping, buried deep in the mud. Be careful—if you wake it up, it might get grumpy!First SparkA strange Hummin has appeared beside the pit where Tucking escaped. Did you just hear it speaking like a person?Brightbough PlateauA perfumer somewhere in Rosetower Woods?Nest of StarsThere should be Aniimo in the Homebuilding Zone too.Ask Emberpup’s owner what happened.Chat with #npcName#.The young girl Leah is always looking around the Tideblossom Coast during the day, as if searching for something. What is she searching for... a lighthouse? But where is there even a trace of a lighthouse nearby?Clue: The Perfumer Looks AnxiousAmethyst GlideContact Dr. Lewis and ask what happenedCatch a Blessed Budclaw and collect Lumin Amber.Clue: A Sorrowful Cloud?Crystal CavernAs the sun and moon pass over the golden woods, winds from the distant plains leave their mark on the ancient stone walls. Beneath the stillness, something remains sealed within the ruins.Pranky from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Investigate the strange Hummin’s secretGlide to the green checkpoint while twined with a CelestisCheck the Piano Steps.Clue: A Bolty on the Phone?Talk to Velouria.A BBQ shop that sells various buff items.Follow Nicole.Echoback HopWait for the next stage to open.EditorCommon.Editor.CustomActionDataCrimson isles hum with the Echoback Songs.Talk to Dr. LewisTwine with the <style=Hint_BgD>Flutternym family</style> and venture deeper into Lumenfly Valley.Into the MistRumor: The Turning of the StarsLunara seems to have found somethingTreasures of the Sea and Where to Find Them (5)At the highest point of the layered peaks, an ancient massive cube still stands atop the mountain. Legend says this was once a sacred place, though those who once came here are long gone.A rare flower seems to have bloomed on the shore...Raise your character to level 40.Is that... a powerful Thornblade up ahead?Ten Colorless Dreams have appeared around the Iris sprout. Perhaps the legendary perfume carrying the color of the land can give them color.Touch the dream blossom and listen to Velouria’s dream.Cornet from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Hummin from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!A unique Aniimo nest found only in the Lost Isles. You may be able to dig up a precious <style=Hint_BgL>Umbrabow Egg</style> here.Advance to Student IIThe Fentufts are picking on a Nimbi?Talk to the curator.Look for the one wearing a big hat.While chatting with the Emberpups, you notice an eavesdropper.Raise your character to level 25.Rumor: Thorn of the StormAre the Budsquires having a tea party?Find the mysterious painter Sorora at Echoback Landing.On Crescendo Cliff in Argent Strait, the perfumer Zephyro and his Flutternym partner are singing to a flower, seemingly trying to make it bloom. If neither Zephyro nor Flutternym can make it bloom with their song, whose voice can?Find a buyer for the famous painting Afternoon of the Blue Furball.Catch an Emberpup!Head to the next checkpoint!Mysterious Chests are scattered all across Idyll. They may be luggage left behind by travelers, supplies stashed by adventurers, or treasures sealed away by ancient people... all waiting to be discovered and opened.In Driftwise Meadow, there are strange clouds that make everyone feel sad. Within these clouds, there seems to be... an upset Nimbi?Flutternym from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Equip an Aniimo with an accessory.Defeat the Alpha Glynsera.Place a Heat Furnace around the Woodland.Keep using the Emberpup’s Fire Bolt to attack until the vines are ignitedTalk to the scared Emberpup.Use a Lightning skill to charge the batteries and power the fan.Find the legendary perfume: Heartfire Orange.Talk to XX.Explore the interior of Whiterose Tower.Join the midnight concertNow, head to the green checkpoint ahead!Complete the required quests in Elite Training Chapter 2.A flower that can’t wait to grow up?Clue: The Unhappy PerfumerRaise your character to level 50.Do you want to try waking up Tucker?The Hummin have gone home. Chat with Witchin.Try perfumer Marlowe’s new product!What happened there?Polaris Institute: Main HallWarning: Omega Aniimo<BR>Danger Level: HighDiscuss your takeaways from the adventures with Dr. Lewis.Talk to Fantine.Approach and touch the lumin amber, then pick up all lumin energyGo to the Institute and find Dr. Lewis.Bloomville is a place of gentle beauty, where petals sway in the morning light and a fleeting moment of wonder can be captured among the flowers.The broken patterns on the three monoliths have sparked much curiosity, yet the power hidden within them remains undiscovered.Outer Eye CornersXiaohongshu Pop-Up StoreCastle Architect - The Architect’s RequestArmsTwine with a Susuta and swim across the river to the finish gate.RV Park: Sea of Flowers - not activatedHelp Rookey recover the lost Helmut.Find Selens. Find the eavesdropper.Elite Pathfinder Challenges are open to the Institute’s most promising students. Each challenge pits you against an academy-certified elite Pathfinder with an outstanding record. Passing proves your strength and earns you an exclusive Institute badge and rare resources.Follow the light path forward.Find Senior Sheepy.Ear HeightTwine with an Aniimo from the Bonesky family.Go to Bloomville and find Perfumer Ranka.Level Helion up to Level 15Burn the vines blocking the way and get to the next checkpointCheck: No Flameheart StoneTalk to Jojo.There seems to be a zealous painter in Horizon Square of Astra...Look for clues about the eavesdropperIs there some connection between the cliffs?Check the Lumen.Find the Flameheart Stone at the summit of the Russet Highlands. It seems to be near something big and dangerous. Be careful!Put in 3 large StarinesReturn 3 StarinesStarry FlowAn item shop that sells Aniimo training items.After the old Sherro returned to the stars, the peace along the shore was shattered.The painter at Echoback Landing seems to be searching for new inspiration.Enter your Homeland.Say goodbye to ShellyTalk to the Elder and attend the festival.The Bloomville perfumer Ranka spends all his time lying motionless on the ground.An Outpost for Pathfinders to take a rest and report the Aniimo they’ve caught.Head to the green target ahead.A makeshift boat made from a giant Aniimo egg.
You can <style=Hint_BgL>deliver eggs</style> or <style=Hint_BgL>leave</style> the island here.Sanctum: Wings UnfurledTwine with an Emberpup and head to the green target point.Omega Aniimo: SherroInvestigate the Pranky on the west side of the park.Talk to Dr. Lewis about the results.Burn the vines blocking the path and enter the valley!Rumor: The Argent Strait Research NotesClue: A Little Flower?Twine with or release Tubster.Defeat Wendell again and earn the badge: Sonata of the WindThis Area is rich in Veins, Bonding large numbers of Aniimo to appear Over Time!Defeat Tucking and obtain the Super Truffle.Home Unlock Story Starting PointRushing RapidsRumor: The Tideblossom Coast Research NotesPillar PuzzleCatch a Susuta!Starwish Coin Exchange CounterFind the treasure of the Russet Highlands: the <style=Hint_BgL>Flame Flower</style>.Climb to the Stormy SummitReturn the leaf to SkippyThe painter Sorora from the Russet Highlands seems to be looking for the "Broken Helmet."Upgrade the RV to level 7.Warning: Alpha Aniimo
Danger Level: MediumTravel back to Astra (no handbook entry).Game Spud has landed in Astra, and the pop-up store event is live for a limited time! Come check it out!Smash Through!Claim the reward for Elite Training Core Courses Chapter 8.Twine with a Helmut.Perfumer Marlowe of Bloomville often produces unusual creations. A new product trial? Why not call it "Only for the Brave"?Head to the green checkpoint aheadLook for the shining shellDr. Glass is waiting for you deep inside the Budsquire maze!See how Rosetower Woods has transformed.Woods GlideAcross the CanyonSwitch the Aniipod Maker to E-mode.Defeat the Inferlupa.Seek friend with the flute once.Find the missing white NimbiRun, Emberpup!Snowy Mountain RunClue: the Inferlupa's Flying Head?Place farmland in your Home.Popota from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Talk to Principal Oswen and Nicole.The two Helmut seem to be troubled by something.Complete 4 required quests in Chapter 2.Panpanta from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo at night to complete the investigation and earn points!Catch 1 Alpha Aniimo.Give the flame flower to Cress.Gather the vine core in the western swamp.It is said that in the Maze of Thorns of the Rosetower Woods lives Melloblum, leader of the Budsquire clan. It possesses the special ability of the Dance of Blissful Bloom, which not only brings joy to all but also restores life to the land. However, the young Princess Melloblum seems to be in some trouble.Chat with the grumpy Chirpi.Jawlings are native to the Russet Highlands, and their unique eyes let them see the world differently.Obtain the regional badgeHorizontalOn a bright, clear day, why is Clovis, the young flower grower of Bloomville, so worried over a single little flower?Practice the song.Return to Sherro’s beach at nightHelion seems to have found somethingEvery legendary perfume tells a story, its scent shaped by the colors and spirit of the earth.Sonic GlideSearch for treasure.Go back to the NorthsideEvacuation PointLook for where the Flutternyms gather.Advance to Wayfarer IIAs time passes, grand halls crumble into ruin. Among the broken walls by the cliff, traces of the past can still be seen.Clue: A Weepy Budsquire Tea Party?Helmut being carried through the air in Helgon’s jawsWin at the Sonic Boom Arena!Offer the Melancholic Fluff.An RV Park by a lake in Driftwise Meadow. Pathfinders can rest, make friends, decorate their camping platforms, gain Park Buffs and send Aniimo on quests in there. <style=Hint_BgL>Find Park Manager Yu to activate it</style>.Talk to Senior Cecelia.Give color to the Colorless Dream: Thousand-Fang.In Beast Fang Ridge, the Bonesky Family and the Emberpup Family have long been locked in a territorial dispute, with neither side willing to back down. A Fenrier has been lingering along the border between their territories. What is it trying to do?Fire By WindHelmut from today’s Field Notes list can be found living near this Track point. Catch the corresponding Aniimo to complete the Field Notes and earn score rewards!Talk to WendellInvestigate the Voxel CoreThe pines whisper softly, flowers dance in the breeze.Sanctum: Rigged MazeBurn out all the vines covering the wall, and climb to the finish gate.Discuss tomorrow’s plan with Nicole.The Icho’s Request?Tuckin of the Mistwoods. Every tree and blade of grass in the forest is an extension of its power.Follow Fannie and take a tour of her RV.Complete 4 required quests in Chapter 4.Mudstone PassGather <style=Hint_BgL>Stoneflower Dew</style>.An angry Fenrier is pacing near the icy-fire border of Beast Fang Ridge.Rumor: The Beast Fang Ridge Research Notes IISearch deep in the Mistwoods for the Super Truffle. Could the finest truffle be hiding near the legendary Tucking...?A unique Aniimo nest found only in the Lost Isles. You may be able to dig up a precious <style=Hint_BgL>Darkler Egg</style> here.Shelly from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Wait for the Harvest Gathering to begin.Talk to Sunia.An RV Park on an island beach in Echoback Landing. Pathfinders can rest, make friends, decorate their camping platforms, gain Park Buffs and send Aniimo on quests in there. <style=Hint_BgL>Find Park Manager Sesa to activate it</style>.Irisal, absorbed in the stage performance, shifts and freezes dance poses to her own rhythm. She can fully control the plants within the “stage” range, shaping them into whatever form she desires.<BR>Refresh interval: 20sAre you looking at the sea?Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Glimmer.A counter where you can exchange for Starwish Coins.A vehicle rests upon Nimbus Fields...From the cliff’s edge, the sea rocks beside the isle come into view. Faint ancient Lumin Amber markings can be seen among them, each one tracing the path of history.Talk to Loulla and switch to night.Twine with <style=Hint_BgD>Iris</style> and dance with other Irises.-137962771Mouth CornersBy the frozen lake, white snow lies deep and still.If the "Rusty Iron Sword" carries the courage of the legendary Pawney, then the "Broken Helmet" seems to carry its friendship with the painter Sorora. Find the "Broken Helmet" and give it to Sorora.Meet Fannie at the agreed-upon location.Only at low tide will its full form be revealed.="This is"&J55&", detailed description for self-modification"OfferThe Blitz Tree is a unique symbol of Blitzwood, with lightning constantly striking near it. At night, special visitors seem to come quietly.A tenacious Minespine. Earthbound power pulses endlessly amid the jagged crystals lining its back.<BR>Respawn interval: 20sWidthBeneath the swaying shadows of this ancient tree, a Lumin treasure lies hidden.Green ShadeSea of Flowers: Not ActivatedGo to the Institute and ask Dr. Bohr for more informationAdventurous Cozite - The Fierce WisptisGo check beneath the Blitz Tree during the day.Who are those gulls?Voxel Coins can be used for a prize draw.EyelinerRumor: A New KnightLook around for cluesWhy was a Budsquire there? Looks like it ran away from Rosetower Woods. Were they being pursued by something very threatening?Visit Pawprint Shop in Astra Square and trade for a few mysterious finds...The Sherro of Echoback Landing patrols the narrow coastline with sword and shield in hand, striding across the waves.Let’s draw out those Hummin!Rumor: Ice and FireCatch up to BINI #9!Go to the next green checkpointChallenge Senior Aster.Prepare for the theory assessmentI have found it.Go to the Perfume Workshop and find Sunia to craft SpicesB's Third SnuggleTalk to Dr. GlassAt the Helmut Habitat, the painter Sorora is troubled by a blurry painting. What kind of riddle is "A ghost swings a sword at a dragon"?Helmut says Infergon is guarding the Sword of Bravery at the mountaintop. A dragon and a sword... that has to be connected to Sorora’s painting. Now Helmut is rushing up the mountain, hoping to pull out the sword while Infergon is distracted. Can it really pull this off?Proceed to the target position!Clue: Colorless Dream: TornadoWaistIs there some kind of pattern on the pillar ahead?Emberpup from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Received a call from Dr. LewisAbove the Driftwise Meadow, a flock of joyful Fentufts tirelessly pass their happiness on to sorrowful Nimbis. Even so, they too grow weary. Whenever this happens, the Fentufts return to their “old home,” Softdown Wilds, to recharge. Just what kind of place is it? And might Perfumer Fantine finally find a kindred spirit there?Talk to Ranka.Talk to Prof. BohrSoil and stone have buried the ancient path, while grass and trees have hidden the traces of human activity, leaving only silent ruins behind.Continue the prerequisite quest.Icho has prepared a special course for you: discover what fighting truly means and become a true warrior. To do that, you’ll need to explore the legends of Beast Fang Ridge. <style=Hint_BgL>Go to Beast Fang Ridge and complete the prerequisite quest: Warrior.</style>An RV Park between the romantic Sea of Flowers and a pine forest. Pathfinders can rest, make friends, decorate their camping platforms, gain Park Buffs and send Aniimo on quests in there. <style=Hint_BgL>Find Park Manager Ben to activate it</style>.LengthFind Sunia at the square and say goodbye.Graceful and elegant, Glameep lingers in the dreamlike mirror lake, gazing at its own reflection as it quietly guards the fading echoes of the past.Dr. Lewis seems to have more to tell you.Switch to NightGive the Bittersweet Dew to Fantine.Ask the mysterious figure about their intentionsWhy has Perfumer Fantine come here? She seems to be worried about something... Should you try comforting her?Island LandingObserve the helmet.Enter the Amethyst Tree.Clue: Zealous PainterCheck what’s wrong with the Amethyst Tree.Find out what’s troubling Sayn.Who is the eavesdropper? They seem to have left something behind. Do you wish to investigate the eavesdropper’s secret further?This island seems to belong to the Scar-faced Helgon, but why are there ancient murals of the Infergon here? The three stone pedestals along the shore also appear in the murals. Is it just a coincidence, or are there still secrets on this island waiting to be uncovered?Lumin Marking: Lake-Center BubbleRising FlameDeliver the notes found in the Forest of Falling Stars to Sayn.Use Spatial Counters to defeat the Budclaw!Cliff VistaShortcut to the CastleDrawn by the bond between humans and Aniimo, Sparkelf has arrived in Astra from SylphIsle!Head to the gateway at the finish point and complete the tutorial courseDefeat the Susuta!Cooperate with wild Aniimos, activate the bouncing plants, and reach the gate at the high destinationThere seems to be some kind of pattern on the whale bone.Clue: Colorless Dream: EchobackWhiterose TowerBulbly is thinking hard.Clue: Perfumer Avetine’s TroublesSay goodbye to Dael.Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Echoback.Rumor: A Broken Helmet?Go to the Russet Highlands and search for the Incense of Courage.Susuta from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Rumor: The Eavesdropper IGive color to the Colorless Dream: Echoback.Core DescentContinue the Mysterious Presence quest.Clue: The Miraculous SeedlingGive color to the Colorless Dream: Glimmer.Listen to Helmut’s whispers.Gather Voxel Coins from the Celestis’s tail.Twine with a Scorchhowl to ignite the vines with Fire BoltComplete the required quests in Elite Training Chapter 4.FunPlus.WorldX.Quest.QuestCustomTriggerDataQuest: The WarriorTorso="This is"&J60&", detailed description for self-modification"Charge the batteries, then watch the metal crate conduct electricity and power the fan.The towering iceberg is dusted with fine snow, its layers glowing with a cool pale-blue sheen like frozen crystal.Ask Celestis what it wants.Make the gears rotateTwine with an Aniimo!Clue: A Perfumer Who Ventured Deep into Danger?Set fire to the tall grass to produce a wind field and ride the wind to the platform above.Put out the fire and head to the next checkpoint.Clue: Dragon Legends IIFrozen StoneYou are leaving Bloomville. Find Sunia at the perfumery and say goodbye.Go to the center to investigateGather the Butterfly Shadows scattered by the dream blossom.Ruins of FlowersGive the Burst of Red to Cress.Though the statue on the grassland has weathered countless years, its eagle-sharp gaze still watches the distance, as if fixed on something unseen.Purchase Lun Dew Carrot SeedsCollapsed CorridorThe old Omega Sherro once said that when the stars return to the sea, they will one day fill the night sky again. A few days have passed since then. Have the Aniimo on the beach learned to coexist peacefully? And is that little Shelly still as prone to tears as before?Show the Broken Helmet.Take out 7 StarinesHipThis is ≪J67≫. Please modify the description manually.Answer Dr. Lewis’s call.The show’s starting! Head over to the stage and snap a selfie with the performing Aniimo!Capture the Moment Budclaw is StunnedClue: A Great Menace?Russet Highlands is the most dangerous area on the entire continent—be prepared and be careful!Look up into the sky, and its shape will appear.Why would the Budsquire have a tea party at Wildflower Cottage on a sunny day?Frostlit TraceA very rare Chest, often hiding something good insideWait until <style=Hint_BgL>tomorrow (real time)</style>.Track Point 2Zephyro, the perfumer, gazes at the Bell of Freedom by the cliffside and murmurs to himself.An item shop that sells various toy items.Bolty from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Omega Aniimo: TuckinPomegg from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!The sturdy and steady Tubster stands firm against the wind and waves along the coast.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sHigher, Faster, the Bolty Dr. Glass Challenge!Courageous WitThe reappearance of the legend of Pawney seems to have brought about some changes.What kind of past does the strongest Scorchhowl Icho have? Perhaps some of the natives of Beast Fang Ridge know a thing or two.Challenge Jilly and complete the assessmentLook for where the Irises gather.Deliver 7 StarinesUse the sketched clues to find the right Aniimo.Follow Nicole on a tour of the InstituteHelp the senior a little moreAt night, Beast Fang Ridge grows quiet and eerie, making it perfect for visiting Pathfinders to explore. You notice that several Emberpups seem to be deliberately guiding you toward the dead forest, but they don’t appear hostile. Since that’s the case, why not go along with it?Shaded StoneIn the Outpost, there is an Aniimo researcher named Sayn sitting on a chair.Lately, holo-equipment failures have been occurring frequently across Astra, and people have even reported seeing something... strange. Just what is going on?ThighsUse a Water skill to activate the Bouncy Pad, then bounce up to the next checkpoint.-1116472677On the second night, you heard the legend of the Undefeated Warrior. Just like the night before, an "eavesdropper" was secretly listening in. That’s where the second night’s story ends. What will the third night reveal? If you’re curious too, wait quietly for the next night to arrive. <style=Hint_BgL>Real time: 1 day later.</style>Beachside SandbarsExplore Idyll!Speak with RonShoulderWhy does Helmut hide out in its Habitat? Why is it so obsessed with the "arm wrestling" game?Use Fire to melt ice and head to the next checkpoint.Hide! Sneak! Operation: Mushroom Hunt!Twine with EmberpupDefeat Wally again and earn the badge: Spring of LifeFind the legendary perfume: Freedom’s Breeze.Lower Eyelid AngleA Bubbeep gathering spot. The Bubbeep here are living their best lives, blowing bubbles and soaking up the sun!At Twister Peaks, on the Stormy Summit, lies Infergon’s most treasured treasure.Castle Architect - The Apprentice Builder’s TroublesAskTwine with a Shelly and get to the checkpoint aheadCapture the EmberpupMomo has brought back an Aniimo Egg...?Learn about Held ItemThe patterns on the stone flicker in and outSet the farmland recipe to Wheat.Clue: A Lighthouse?Deliver the “Anonymous Research Notes” to Sayn.Keep patrolling with the Sparkly ShellyActivate the Branch.Find the legendary perfume: Whisper of Longing.Determine: Possess Echoback SaltShipwreck BayAria told you the story of "Flowers and Thorns" without charging a fee. Instead, she asked you to look after Awen if you meet her in Rosetower Woods. Who is Awen, and what does she mean to Aria?The aloof Geoclaw bears glowing crystal amber on its back, beautiful yet dangerous.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sA group of Shellies lives here, and one of them seems to be special.Complete 100 orders in your Homeland.Capture complete, talk to Nicole!Find or own a <style=Hint_BgL>Tubster</style>.Give the Maple Candy Apple Jam to Jojo.Deliver vine cores.Go back to Bloomville with Sunia after your exploration.Use the Call Friends command to summon wild ShellyBattle Senior LoullaDouble EyelidsLook for Sunia.Plant wheat on your farmland plots.Shrubclaw from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Bloomville holds an odd perfumer named Ranka. He always lies around lazily and never gets to his scent-making work. What keeps him idle?Twine with a Susuta-family Aniimo.Snow Mountain RunAsk Bohr.Track down the food-loving Hummin.Use Scorchhowl’s Drop Kick to smash through the floor and reach the next target point.MatteThe high-spirited Wolfkin fighter, <BR> driven by its competitive nature, gets even more Boiling Blood the stronger the Opponent it faces. For fire and cinders leave the marks of its growing strength. <BR>Refresh Interval: 20 secondsReach the AreaClues: The Fanatical PainterTalk to the mysterious Aniimo.Talk to Pippi's owner.Magmarex lurks deep within the cavern, where fierce heat surges through the crimson crystals covering its body.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sBeneath the green canopy, a cool breeze stirs, and a mysterious pattern can just be seen on the great tree.Gate of RuinsHead to Tideblossom Coast to visit Irelia.Listen to Emberpup tell... a ghost story at night?Hurry—go see what’s happening!Gather the vine core in the northern cave.This is a Sanctum, modify the specific description as neededThe Frizzy Old Bolty tells you that if you’re curious about what other Bolties are thinking, you can hide behind the Blitz Tree at night and listen in. The way it acts so mysteriously suggests these visitors are no ordinary guests.Talk to the enlarged Scorchhowl.Talk to Nicole.Talk to Senior CeceliaComplete 3 required quests in Chapter 7.Use the Carousel Mill to process Wheatmeal once.Sing with the Windgliders.Go to the Sea of FlowersSomething strange seems to be happening in Astra’s Northside...Return to Outpost and report to Dr. LewisTalk to Icho about the legend of Beast Fang RidgeExamine Senior Aster.Veilfloat that watches the seaDefeat the Infergon and revive the Pawney’s legend.Chat with the gulls.Upgrade the RV to level 4.Northern Woodland of the Flower SeaAfter searching, a large number of target Aniimo were found here. Come quickly for Field Notes!Discuss the Meaning of Battle with the Icho.Find out why the Bittersweet Bloom won’t blossom.Upgrade RV to level 10.Upgrade the RV to level 3.This is a wilderness Alpha. Edit the detailed description as needed.What did Perfumer Zephyro leave behind?Touch the strange blossom.Listen to Fannie introduce another facility.After that landslide, the Berylline Vale gained a track that seemed to “fall from the sky.” Countless Baleetles have come from far and wide to race down it, yet no one knows the true origin of the track. Go and talk to that old Bouldus wandering around in search of a stone ball! It witnessed how it all began.Defeat Flameruff · The Mighty and obtain the Unbroken Flameruff SpiritAsk around about the Inferlupa.The Branch that grows in Breezy Plains seems attuned to the surrounding ecosystem. As its energy grows, the Branch’s hidden treasures can be unlocked.Show the photo to Cozite.Urban railway entrance/exit of AstraFannie has refreshed the Home Shop.Use the fan's airflow to reach the higher platform and arrive at the final gateDefeat the Turbo.Go to ChillBeanz and look for Lucas.AnglePerfumer Fantine stands by the river, seemingly weighed down by something.Amid this sea of green grass, the stone pillar and the ruined gate behind it speak of an ancient legend. When the pillar and gate become one, a story long sealed by time begins to unfold.Flameruff from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Clue: Colorless Dream: CrescendoGo to Echoback Landing and search for the scent of renewal and return.Get to the checkpoint within the tall grassSurfing in the Sea of FlowersCollect Lumin Amber before heading to the Branch.Give the salt to Sunia.Use Explosive Barrels to blast through the rubble, then head to the finish line.Deliver 5 large StarinesB's First SnuggleAn Aniipod store that sells Aniipods of different grades.Irises with six regional formsHelp the anxious NimbiIf the "Rusty Iron Sword" carries the courage of the legendary Pawney, then the "Broken Helmet" seems to carry its friendship with the painter Sorora. Find the "Broken Helmet" and deliver it to Sorora.Collect your RV.Perfumer Avetine wants her apprentice to graduate soon so she can head off on a happy journey. But her apprentice doesn’t seem to be catching on, and that’s driving her mad. Right now, she needs the help of a skilled Pathfinder like you!Go here to find Tucking.Forgotten MineClue: Echoback’s SongAdvance to Wayfarer IIILook for Voxel Coins outside Shanel.Navigate to the front desk.Find the eavesdropper.Wake Shelly <style=Hint_BgL>(try using shock waves)</style>.Twine with a Susuta!Find the Inferlupa research notes on Beast Fang Ridge.Quietly blend in with the Emberpup family.Grizbo, gentle by nature, chooses to live in solitude to avoid harming its companions, sealing its ferocious side deep within a mountain cave.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sEyeshadowAbundant fire elements have stained these rock walls their distinctive russet hue.Did Budsquire’s brother, who left on a stormy day, become Thunderstorm Thornblade?Return to Outpost and find Dr. LewisYou don’t have enough Aniipods. Go find Nicole.Lumin Marking: Veiled TruthStonebound SwordRumor: The Perfect RacerProtected by an unknown power, the ice in the cave remains frozen for eternity. A faint Lumin Amber pattern can be seen through the ice, whispering tales from a forgotten age.The elegant and dignified Leafy lives in ponds blanketed with lotus leaves.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sIcho, the Scorchhowl at Dr. Lewis’s side, has opened a course to seek out the “true meaning of the warrior.” The answer seems to lie among Thousand-Fang Ridge. Do your best to explore the story of the Inferlupa! When you find more clues, perhaps Icho will want to talk with you.The ingredients are ready. It’s time to visit Velouria.Check the platform board.Observe the tombstone.Progress through Story Quests to unlock the day/night Switch feature.Give the Treasured Large Starine to DaelAn RV Park between Nimbus Fields and Mistwoods. Pathfinders can rest, make friends, decorate their camping platforms, gain Park Buffs and send Aniimo on quests in there. <style=Hint_BgL>Find Park Manager Umi to activate it</style>.Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Crescendo.Give another Starine to the manager of the Starwish Gacha.Lower Eyelid FoldWhere sea breeze and gull cries rise together, thorn-covered rocks stand at the edge of the shore, as if guarding hidden secrets and treasure.Go to the Sea of Flowers and find Wally.B's Second SnuggleLocated on the second floor of Polaris Institute’s main hall, it is an internal area of the institute that connects core departments including Aniimology, Pathfinding, and Battle Art.Explore this mysterious place.Test your strength with Coilstrike Coupons on this Coilstrike Strength Tester for surprising rewards.Bloom - White SandbankSearch for <style=Hint_BgL>Golden Answer</style>.Twine with Shelly and head to the Uncommon checkpoint aheadCastle Architect - The Apprentice Builder’s DilemmaAsk the repairer nearbyRotationContinue to collect Voxel CubesTell Senior Wally what you foundLumin Marking: Fragment RestorationThis is ≪J67≫ — edit the description freely.Chat with the Fentuft Inspector.The perfumer at the entrance of the Celestis outpost?Defeat Loulla again and earn the badge: Darknight StarTry catching the Emberpup!Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Thousand-Fang.Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Tornado.Petal ShoresOwn 1 Aniimo with Resonance at Tier 2.Perfumer Dael is anxiously looking at the Nest of Stars.Sanctum: Water to IceKeyhole SightDuring the day, many Baleetles gather at Berylline Vale, and on sunny days, they race about without a care in the world. At this moment, Baleetle Jenny is standing in the middle of the road, staring blankly at a beautiful mud ball. What’s going on?Ask Prof. Bohr for adviceThis is ≪J67≫ — description editable at your discretion.When the ruined structures become one, you may glimpse the glory this place once knew.Soak the wooden chest so it becomes conductive, then activate the fan.Give color to the Colorless Dream: Crescendo.Go to the top of the mountain and find more information about the legend of PawneyGive the new Shell Shovel to SusutaDeliver 10 StarinesReturn to Bloomville.Clue: Colorless Dream: BeryllineVerticalA group of wretched Budsquires?Find Awen.Nurture the ecosystem 40 times in the Breezy Plains.Adventurous Cozite - Destination: Mystery Island!A group of Budsquires are sharing lore over a pot of tea in the Wildflower Cottage. If you have the time, go have a listen.BridgeFind the Hummin lost in the forest {0}/5Visit Wendell in Zephyrus LandbridgeWisptis from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Greet the elder.Submit OrderShow the Tubster what freedom feels like.Lumin Marking: Above the White CliffsChat with Fantine.Cliff MarkTalk to Zephyro and help the Bell of Freedom bloom.Decorate your personal platform once.Find the Fragrant Emberpup.Starlit blooms weave a velvet green beneath your feet.Use Gravity Pull to move the obstacle aside, then head to the green target point.Listen in on the nearby conversation.All three ingredients have been gathered. Now go back to Bloomville Perfume Workshop and find Sunia to craft the ancient perfume.Perform Capability Awakening for Aniimo 5 timesOwn Rock in your Home warehouse.Go find Dr. Lewis at the outpost and complete the quiz.Use the Emberpup’s Fire Bolt to ignite the vines blocking the wayShow Roar of the BouldusTry to sense the Colorless Dream: Falling Stars.Keep collecting Crystals and head to the Sacred Tree.As the tide strikes the shore, traces of ancient ruins can be glimpsed between the white surf and pink reefs.Hosts, guests, and uninvited visitors all came and went in haste, leaving behind nothing but a scene of desolate neglect.Place an Element Essence.Go to the Sanctum.Quick DiveActivate the Bloom in Bloomville.“Anonymous Research Notes”Stay at the elder’s house for the night.Check the Aniimo’s status in your Home.Upgrade a level 1 farmland plot to level 2.Use a Water skill to activate the Bouncy Pad and bounce off of it to the checkpoint.North of Horizon SquareSet your Woodland recipe to Cherry Blossom.Help your Emberpup evolve into a Flameruff.Transmit data to the Voxel CoreFly to the Somniwing’s throne.Wait for Senior Aster to wrap up his pre-battle preparations.Jojo reviews every task on the festival checklist.Head to Astra plaza and set off fireworks for the Starlight Festival!Mysterious visitors seem to come beneath the Blitz Tree at night to share their troubles.Holo-Device Malfunction - CaféContinue to move to the green target pointFreshsprout HillClue: The Aging SherroFind the research notes scattered around the Forest of Falling Stars.Float DownEchoback Landing: Not ActivatedTalk to the Bulbly by the cliff.Complete 4 required quests in Chapter 1.Find a buyer for the famous painting Pointillist Hatching Melody.Lumin Marking: Gate of RuinsCheekbonesGo to Arlo to process the aromathysts.Look for the host, Oscar, at Horizon Square.Ancient canopies weave a dark green dome, scattering daylight into moss-cracked hollows, where silent eyes watch passing travelers.Give Pranky an ideaIs that... <style=Hint_BgL>Jenny?</style>Ask Emberpup what it wants.Lumin Marking: Northern Woodland of the Flower SeaSet the time to <style=Hint_BgD>night</style> and get ready to rest.Go to Bloomville and chat with Grace.Drive away the <style=Hint_BgL>Susuta family</style>.Find the mud ball’s owner.Meet Your Fire CompanionDiscover why the Melloblum can no longer dance.Raise your character to level 60.Talk to Irelia.Give the "Broken Helmet" to Sorora.Catch a <style=Hint_BgD>Dewy</style>.Help the fragrant Emberpup obtain the <style=Hint_BgL>Flareburst Flowers</style>.Show Pointillist Hatching Melody.Search for the Super Truffle.Find a <style=Hint_BgL>Tromber</style> willing to join the band.Explore the idol ruins.Here in the Iris habitat, the seedlings are transformed. Yesterday, they turned dun, like the earth. Today, they’re painted with colorless dreams? A cycle of colors, a cycle of intent?Inject energy into the Branch in Breezy Plains a total of 30 times.Deliver “Research on the Bonesky Species” to Sayn.Rumor: Nighttime VisitorVisit Senior Xiaochen in Rosetower WoodsThe honest and gentle Panpantas can unleash astonishing strength when defending its nest.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sCatch an Iris!Electronic music pulses through the arena, and cheers rise wave upon wave. On the arena stage, matchups shift in an instant, and extreme plays keep igniting the crowd. This is the art of battle, and the carnival of rhythm!Find a buyer for the famous painting Roar of the Bouldus.Ask Selene.Clue: Perfume, New Product Promotion!Legend has it that on the shore of Echoback Landing at night, the graceful song of Echoback can be heard. Those who hear the Echoback’s song receive a blessing from the deep sea. And the mysterious painter by the shore seems to be searching for that very song...Learn how to make perfumes from Sunia.NostrilsBound for Bloomville.Talk to Senior Wally.Hide here.Let’s look for the mysterious painter Sorora.Go talk to Bohr by the Holographic Discovery Booth.Search for the truth behind “the Inferlupa’s flying head” at night.Use the Bouncy Pad in the water again to reach the platform, then head to the finish gate.On the first night, you defeated an Inferlupa that seemed to have lost all will to fight. Then, by the bonfire outside Thousand-Fang Ridge, you heard the legend of the Lost Warrior. There was also a very obvious "eavesdropper." That’s where the first night’s story ends. What will the second night reveal? If you’re curious too, wait quietly for the next night to arrive. <style=Hint_BgL>Real time: 1 day later.</style>Catch AreaFly Over the ValleyGo to Idyll.Listen to Helmut's secret whisper.Salt wind and Chirpi songs weave through the fjord in endless delight.Clue: Colorless Dream: GlimmerSclera ColorPerfumer Awen seems to be looking for something.Find the Pranky holding a leafFly back to the nest and craft duskwhisper aromathysts.Progress the main quest to unlock the Day and Night Switch feature.Use the item to restore Scorchhowl’s size.Go to the second floor to rest.Deliver the Flareburst Flower.Built by the lake, it’s the hub of the whole Northside that connects different shopping streets.Open 30 Chests in the World cumulatively.Try waking Tucker up?Lumin Marking: Cliff MarkScatter the fragrance and enter the Amethyst Tree.Use the Pathfinder’s Hammer Strike to break through the stone wall and reach the next target point.Touch the BloomSprint UphillClue: Eternal RedClimb the wall to the high ground while twined with a CelestisTalk to the mysterious painter.Flickering shadows mask an ancient wonder.Discuss the collectible found in the chest with JillyLead the wild Shelly you called over to the checkpoint by the Bouncy Pad.Find or own a <style=Hint_BgL>gull that can handle the Basso</style>.The seedling seems to have changed.Return to your RV Park.Princess Melloblum seems to know you...?Clue: Dragon Legends IPanorama from AfarElvira the perfumer sits by the water, lost in thought. Even Appo the Budclaw can’t seem to ease what’s weighing on her. Can a scent carry longing? Elvira wants to understand the answer her mother once gave.Infuse energy into the Branch in Breezy Plains a total of 5 times.Complete the enrollment ceremonyLook for the one with a golden star on its forehead.Watch the live footage.An enraged Fenrier prowls the border between ice and fire in Beast Fang Ridge.Look at the painting.Find the <style=Hint_BgL>"strange" perfume ingredient</style>.Rumor: Ice and Fire IIChat with the old Bouldus.Budsquire from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!At the border of the Susuta and Shelly habitats roams a uniquely charismatic Susuta.Sanctum: ShatterstoneClue: The Land in Happy BloomGo to the Holo-Lab immediatelyChat with Elvira.Enter Bloomville.I heard this painter is really obsessed with drawing weird shapes, but barely anyone gets it. Maybe they’re waiting for someone who can truly appreciate their work...Go to the perfumery and look for Sunia.Go to the Holo-Lab.Investigate the Pranky in the middle of the park.Omega Aniimo: GlameepCrystal CaveA <style=Hint_BgL>curious Susuta?</style>Clue: Colorless Dream: Falling StarsTwine with <style=Hint_BgD>Dewy</style> and gather Duskwhispers.Take out 10 starinesDepth<style=Hint_BgL>Fight</style> the Inferlupa.Lumin Marking: Cliff VistaBonesky Family ResearchOpen the Farmland Settings screen.Report to Principal OswenRumor: The Aniimo Researcher in a ChairFind some <style=Hint_BgL>Bittersweet Dew</style>.Try catching a Hummin!Take a selfie!Disguise yourself as <style=Hint_BgL>a Helmut</style> bestie.The Infergon of Crimson Peak Forest commands the storms and flames of the mountaintops.Mysterious Chests scattered across Idyll may be luggage left behind by travelers, supplies stashed by adventurers, or even treasures sealed away by the ancients... all waiting to be discovered and opened.Keep Twined with the Celestis and climb the wall to the top.Talk to Elvira.Upper ArmsExplore the Celestis outpost!Talk to the worried PomeggProgress “The Warrior” for more clues.Clue: A Perfumer Lying on the GroundElvira the perfumer seems troubled near the entrance to Bloomville.A café offering all kinds of coffee and specialty drinks. The Star-Crossed Tea Party runs daily from 18:00 to 02:00, with limited items and special benefits up for grabs. We look forward to your visit!Place an Aniipod Maker in your Home.SpreadWhat’s <style=Hint_BgL>beneath the Blitz Tree</style>?Complete Johnny’s <style=Hint_BgL>racing challenge</style>.Twine with a Bonesky and get to the checkpoint ahead.Challenge Wally and complete the assessmentTake out 7 starinesReach the Horizon Square to reset.Grace and Cress are famous perfumers in Bloomville and inheritors of the legendary perfumes. They seem completely different, yet somehow make the perfect perfume-making partners. They also appear to have a hidden connection to the Infergon of the Russet Highlands.Chat with Leah, the girl looking around, in the daytime.A group of Celestises lives here, and one of them seems to be special.Legend has it that when Sherro grows old, it becomes a shooting star and returns to the stars. But why does the Omega Sherro who once commanded the stars refuse to leave? Where does the blade point—at an enemy, or at the starlight it has sworn to protect?Complete the match.Basic ColorThis Aniimo’s friend went missing. Can you help?Use a Water skill to put out the fire and head to the next checkpoint.Sanctum: Chasing StormwindsThe painter Sorora is troubled by a blurry painting.Bring Sunia back.Upper LipUse an ice skill to put out the fire and head to the next checkpointClue: Colorless Dream: LightningYou found Ranka’s partner: a fragrant Emberpup. But to help Ranka create a legendary perfume, it wants to stay in Beast Fang Ridge and obtain Flareburst Flowers. How can you make them bloom again? <style=Hint_BgL>Go to Beast Fang Ridge and complete the prerequisite quest: Warrior.</style>This is a Bloom, specific description can be modified as neededThe mysterious Stellarys streak across the night sky like a meteor.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sVillage VistasRumbling StonesSanctum: Double VisionRail Exit A_Northern Plaza, NorthsideDefeat the enemy!An accessory shop that sells personalized Aniimo accessories.="This is "&J60&", edit the detailed description yourself"The distant cliff face seems to bear a mysterious patternBurn out all the vines covering the wall, and climb to the finish gateGlow IntensityLearn how to switch Aniimo skills!Go here to make a report.Mysterious chests are scattered across Idyll. They may be luggage lost by travelers, supplies left behind by adventurers, or treasures sealed away by an ancient civilization... All of them are waiting to be discovered and opened.Make 1 friend.Complete the required quests in Elite Training Chapter 5.Chat with Cress.Twine with a Budsquire and hit the Cubbo’s rose.A burly and resilient Rookey that uses its thick armor plates to protect its companions.<BR>Respawn interval: 20sAsk the holo-tech engineerHow does it feel?Catch a Flutternym!The scar-faced Helgon wants you to pretend to be a Helmut friend and help its child, Jawling, find the treasure it prepared. Twine with Helmut and go see Jawling.FullnessDeliver the notes found at Tideblossom Coast to Sayn.Go to Echoback Landing and make the whalesong blossoms bloom.Twine with a Dewy and gather nectar at the top of the tower.You helped Sorora recall memories of the Russet Highlands, and heard fragments of the dragon legends. After the earthquake, part of the Russet Highlands became an island, now separated from the highlands by the sea. A Scar-Faced Helgon seems to travel back and forth between the two. Perhaps... you could ask it for help?<style=Hint_BgL>Recommended: a Pawney.</style>Ask Senior Loulla for her thoughts on the concert.Ear TiltThe wind-eroded stone pillars appear to bear mysterious patternsTry catching a Skippy!Place a Crackle Generator in your Home.Find your RV.Own an Iris.Twine with NimbiComplete the required quests in Elite Training Chapter 1.Gather the Incense of Tolerance at Echoback Landing.Dragon’s VisionHead to the Hatos Ruins and find the Broken Helmet.Give the <style=Hint_BgL>Stoneflower Dew</style> to Marlowe.The angry Fenrier is waiting for an Emberpup that can breathe endless fire. Where could it be?Clue: A Strange HumminGo back to Dr. Glass="This is "&J67&", edit the detailed description yourself"A flower-filled town steeped in fragrance, where the residents have practiced Perfumery with the help of Aniimo for generations.Defeat Thunderstorm Thornblade.Hidden in Beast Fang Ridge are clues to the “true meaning of the warrior,” and to Icho’s past.Complete the assessment and report to your instructorFind the legendary perfume: Golden Wish.Talk to Senior Aster.Place Harvest Gathering: Get-Together in the Limited-Time Event Zone.Explore the Rosetower Woods and let the land bloom with joy.Deliver your reply to Ranka.Lock on the Celestis.Rumor: The Beast Fang Ridge Research Notes IGo to Northside and continue collecting Voxel CubesTake a photo of an angry EmberpupMysterious pale violet markings have appeared on the tree stumps hidden deep within the Forest of Falling Stars.Catch a <style=Hint_BgD>Flutternym</style>. A sad Nimbi seems to be... trapped within the gloomy clouds?Go to Bloomville and look for Clovis.Rumor: Awen?Deliver Sherro’s <style=Hint_BgL>shell sword</style>.Condition: No Super TruffleDeliver the Bittersweet Dew.Tucker is sleeping buried in the soil. Be careful—if Tucker wakes up, it might get angry!Give color to the Colorless Dream: Rosetower.Ride the wind to the grassland.Bonesky from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo at night to complete the investigation and earn points!Explore the story of the Bulbly.Maybe Dr. Lewis knows something.Complete the quizRainbow WoodsCheck on the Voxel CubesTake 1 photo with an Aniimo.Challenge Easy Holo-Battle Sim once.Gather <style=Hint_BgL>Bittersweet Dew</style>.Sorora, a painter from the Russet Highlands, seems to be looking for the "Broken Helmet."Why is Perfumer Dael standing by the entrance to the Celestis outpost looking anxious? Is there something bothering him?Go to Jiff’s shop and investigate the anomalyAnimation SpeedFinish the institute tour and make your choiceEnter the valley!Abundant VeinFollow the shooting stars across the night sky to find this Aniimo. Brimming with electricity, it can freely adjust the brightness and frequency of its glow, and its tentacles flash in brilliant colors that reflect its mood.Use normal attacks and skills to BREAK a Celestis then perform a Quick Catch!Rumor: The Eavesdropper IIFind the source of the fragrance.Level Emberpup up to Level 12Reply to the Frizzy Young Bolty.Investigate the empty stone seats.Follow the Emberpup FamilyProgress the “Helmut’s Island Adventure” quest.Lumin Marking: Frostlit TraceGive color to the Colorless Dream: Falling Stars.When a thunderstorm rolls in, a Thunderstorm Thornblade is said to appear outside the ruined house in the Sea of Flowers. He defeats his opponents with indifference, snapping their thorns... but does he remember what he is fighting for? Perhaps he awaits someone to defeat him—to carry away those pale thorns and grant him release.Chat with Marlowe.Meet Fannie at the Co-op Store.Sanctum: First FlameHere in the iris habitat, the seedlings are transformed.Go to Perfumer Dael!Lumin Marking: Keyhole SightUpgrade the RV to level 2.Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Rosetower.Find Sunia at the square.Investigate Irelia’s condition.Find the legendary perfume: Peace of Mind.Ear AngleDefeat the Glynsera in Nighttime Form.When the Fentufts get tired of playing, they run back to their “old home” to flop down and rest.The massive stones stand guarding the ancient woods, the Lumin Amber patterns on them seem bewildering amid the play of light and shadow. The truth lies among the almost identical patterns.Dr. Glass’s research has hit a snag. Twine with a Susuta to help him complete his research!A mysterious pattern emerges on the tree.Ask Senior Loulla for her thoughts on the concertWhat are these marks?Talk to NovaCancel lock-on.You receive a comms call from Fannie.Find a bespectacled NimbiDefeat the First Lethal Thorn.Check on the HelmutDefeat the four Lethal Thorns outside.Give the whitesnow rose aromathyst to Awen.Find the Hummin that loves picking up things.Lumin Marking: Frozen StoneApproach the Celestis till it’s within your attack range then start attacking.Clue: Legends of Beast Fang RidgeDay gives way to night, and another new star rises along the shore.Gather information about the mud ballClovis, the young florist, seems to have become friends with a small flower, which has now developed some unknown issues. Clovis might need your help.Find the legendary perfume: Binding Oath.Look for Elvira the perfumer at the entrance to Bloomville.Found you!Pathfinders can transport from here.Try to sense the Colorless Dream: Driftwise.Baleetle Jenny stands in the middle of the road, staring at a beautiful mud ball.Find the research notes scattered around Driftwise Meadow.Leah has told you that a legend of the Golden Shooting Star can be seen on the Tideblossom Coast at night.Deliver: Treasured Large StarineStarwish GachaSmart GreedlingClear the waste ground.Show Afternoon of the Blue Furball.Find a <style=Hint_BgL>Cornet</style> willing to join the band.Wake Irisal through battle.Upgrade the RV's Power Module to level 1.Talk to the Sparkly ShellyLumin Marking: Whale BoneHelmut left you a clue: a pattern shaped like an eye. What is it trying to say? Is there something hidden in the storm that only Helmut can see?Adventurous Cozite - To the Top of the CastleSanctum: Through Flame and ThornEarn 5,000,000 Home Coins in total.Try using the Emberpup’s Fire Bolt to ignite the vinesAn Emberpup and a Bonesky were lifelong rivals in Beast Fang Ridge. They fought 364 duels, and not once did either of them truly win. So they made a promise: once they became Flameruff and Fenrier, they would return to the same place for one final match. But the Emberpup never came. What happened?Crumbling StonewallsIn Beast Fang Ridge, several Flameruffs · The Mighty gather at Thousand-Fang Ridge during the day, hoping to win a duel and earn the chance to become Scorchhowl.RV Park: Driftwise Meadow - not activatedFind a way into Whiterose Tower.Complete your enrollment.Follow the Prismana flow. It may lead to secrets buried beneath the snow and ice.Explore the legend of Flowers and Thorns in the Maze of Thorns.You revived the Pawney’s legend. Return to Sorora.Look for Blubby on the second floor of ChillBeanz.Own a level 3 woodland plot.Talk to Lita.Check the <style=Hint_BgL>shiny shell</style>.Enter the contest arena (no handbook entry).Ask Dr. Lewis.Say goodbye to SusutaOn a lonely island cut off from the world, a dragon’s treasure lies hidden.Snowy MountainsideTalk to the Susuta from beforeGet Scar-faced Helgon’s "help"Go to Tideblossom Coast and find Senior Cecelia.Go check on Sherro’s beachTalk to #npcName#Practice the song with the gulls.Talk to ClovisFollow the prompt to search for Voxel Coins in Eco Park.Mountain SanctumJoin the Budsquire tea party.Use Gravity Pull to place the batteries into the battery slots and power the fan.Hot Spring ReefGo here to find Outpost Vendor Joff.Sanctum: All in SightUse the Bouncy Pad in the water to reach the finish gate.Take out 10 StarinesA Reefish gathering spot. Don’t be fooled by their coral disguises—find a way to make them pop out of the sand!Sing together.Join Tubster for Windgliders practicePlace a farmland plot in your Home.The dawn’s rosy glow upon a sea of flowers gives Bloomville a unique charm.Arrive at the Sea of Flowers RV Park.Wake up Tucker.A group of Hummins lives here, and one of them seems to be special.A Flame Flower has grown here.Progress the story quest to unlock the day/night switching feature.The wooden stumps in the Forest of Falling Stars seem to bear mysterious patterns.Talk to the fragrant Emberpup.Clue: The Golden Shooting StarReach peak cheerfulness!Clear debris off the festival grounds.The Alpha Scorchhowl training tirelessly beneath the tallest Ridgeback Tree, the honor-scarred Glynsera Recas in the ice cave, and the Ghost Glynsera that turn feral in the ice cave at night... defeat them, and you may uncover many secrets.Use Elemental Counters to defeat the Hummin!Search for the incense of courage and complete the quest [Warrior].Twister PeaksClue: A Perfect... Mudball?Lumin Marking: Shaded StoneClues: Fanatical PainterTry catching a Celestis!Syncing map module...Submit the Stoneflower Dew.JawlinePurchase Waxing Lun Pepper SeedsAn ancient gate rises from the grasslands, its surface etched with primordial designs.Perfumer Marlowe has released a new perfume. Want to try it?Ask Jilly what happenedA curious pattern can be vaguely seen through the ice.Find Ranka’s Emberpup companion.Visit the plaza and inspect the stone statues.Tell Jiff what you foundOutpost hatchinatorGo to Berylline ValeSanctum: Electric SurgeTwine with an Emberpup and move to the green target pointInvestigate the Pranky on the east side of the park.Reach RV level 3.The scar-faced Helgon walks over to one of the stone seats. Is it waiting for someone to arrive?Finish talking to Bohr.Lumin Marking: Petal ShoresPlace a Carousel Mill in your Home.Ride the wind to the green target point on the higher platform.Give the flame flower root to Grace.Lively GreedlingBlend in with the Emberpup familyChirpi Songs Over the FjordSign up with the host, Oscar.Give the Harvest Platter to Jojo.Omega: GlameepCheck out the upgraded RV Park.Plant Cherry Blossoms.Progress through Story Quests to unlock the day/night Switch featureContinue progressing the prerequisite QuestsLumin Marking: Nest of StarsHair BunGather Lumin Amber from the river.Find the clues in the Russet Highlands to fix the painting.The majestic statue seems to be gazing intently at something far awayNimbi from today’s investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Challenge Wendell and complete the assessmentBack outside Lumenfly Valley again?Raise your character to level 65.Twine with Helmut and shatter the Dragonclaw Stone.The patterns in the ruins flicker in and outFind a way to decipher the language of the electric current.Head to Lumenfly ValleyTalk to the angry FenrierAside from the legend of the Golden Shooting Star that appears on the Tideblossom Coast at night, Leah also told the story of her friend, the sailor Hayes. You learned that every time Hayes returned from sea, he would mutter about a “lighthouse.” Leah doesn’t understand why.Own an Emberpup (you can catch one nearby).Deliver the Flame Flower RootYou’ve found the perfumer, Awen.Bouldus’s rugged body conceals a will even tougher than rock—never yielding in a collision.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sAsk Sparki what it wants.Process an item with the Aniipod Maker once.Keep Twined with the Celestis and glide to the green checkpoint.Find the Bonesky research notes in Beast Fang Ridge.Talk to Fannie and Yu.Upgrade the RV’s Ecological Module to level 1.Clue: The Painter of the Russet HighlandsA Popapus gathering spot. At high tide, there’s no way into the cave, so wait and see when the water pulls back.Deliver the notes found at Driftwise Meadow to Sayn.Lumin Marking: Pillar PuzzleThe Rosetower Woods was once covered with white flowers stretching across the hills, dotted here and there with Cubbo's Roses containing miraculous energy. Explore the Maze of Thorns and let the land bloom with joy once more.Lumin Marking: Ruins of FlowersDiscuss festival preparations with Jojo.Ask Sorora if he has finished his paintings.Head to the Blastbeat Arena.Talk to JessicaBridge WidthFind Baleetle Jenny.Clue: Mysterious PresenceTake out 3 StarinesSprinkle fragrance in front of the seedlings.You can draw prizes with Starwish Coins.Clue: The True Meaning of the WarriorSeek out Gurulu near the square dance zone.Place Harvest Gathering: Bright Blooms in the Limited-Time Event Zone.Reach level 25.This island seems to belong to the Scar-Faced Helgon, but why is there an ancient mural of Infergon on the island? The three stone thrones on the shore also seem to appear in the mural. Coincidence? Or does the island still hold secrets you have yet to discover?<style=Hint_BgL>Recommended: a Pawney.</style>Observe the stele.Help the Tubster join the band.Grace hopes you can help find the treasure of the Russet Highlands: the Flame Flower. It seems tied to the legends of the highlands. <style=Hint_BgL>Go to the Russet Highlands and complete the prerequisite quest: Warrior.</style>Call Dr. Lewis.Burn the vines in your way and head to the next checkpoint.Aniimo Researcher Sayn? Sounds impressive! But why is he always sitting there, as if he’s not feeling well?Treasures of the Sea and Where to Find Them (6)Give the Umbral Hot Pot to Jojo.Check: No Echoback SaltAvetine, a perfumer from Bloomville, is offering a high price for an ingredient called Golden Answer. Where could it be? Golden... maybe Blitzwood is worth a look. <style=Hint_BgL>Go to Blitzwood and complete the prerequisite quest: An Answer from the Heavens.</style>There is a group of wretched Budsquires near the entrance of Rosetower Woods.Defeat Velouria.Switch to night.Give color to the Colorless Dream: Tornado.Jeff at Super Claw seems to be looking for help...Prepare to craft fragrance.Lumin Marking: Green ShadeRaise your character to level 70.Upgrade RV to level 20.Three ancient monoliths stand, guarding forgotten memories.CalvesCatch up with Nicole. She’s calling for us!Light the incense and open the barrier to Lumenfly ValleyAfter searching, a large number of target Aniimo were found here. Come quickly to investigate!Harvest and pick up Common Wheat.Head to Softdown Wilds!Lumin Marking: Crumbling StonewallsFind the Emberpup that can breathe endless fireJoin the Helgon and Rookey gathering.Chat with the amazing Jawling.Challenge Senior Cecelia and complete the assessment.RV Park: Nimbus Fields - not activatedOmega at Echoback LandingRumor: The Joyful Old HomeFrom the Emberpup chatter, you learn that only the strongest Scorchhowl can earn the name "Icho." Many elite Flameruffs have gathered at Thousand-Fang Ridge. Maybe they want to become the next Icho, or maybe they want to restore the Ridgeback Tree to the blazing glory it once had.Adventurers can Transport here.MeasurementsSet the farmland to the Quick Wheat recipe.Talk to the Skippy in the caveSanctum: WindborneFantine, a cheerful perfumer from Bloomville, has often been misunderstood for her optimism. Now she has come to Driftwise Meadow, only to find that she cannot understand why her Nimbi companion is so sad. Is it wrong to be happy? The special perfume ingredient found in Driftwise Meadow may help her find an answer. Find a way to make the Bittersweet Blooms blossom. <style=Hint_BgL>Go to Driftwise Meadow and complete the prerequisite quest: Fentufts and the Nimbi.</style>Alpha Aniimo: TurboThis is ≪J67≫. For details, edit it manually.Spread happiness to Big One.Go to Voxel SpaceWatch Sunia create the Aeon incense.Give the Flareburst Flowers to Ranka.Chat with the Scar-faced Helgon.Investigate the holo projector on the roofFannie and Yama say goodbye to me.Massive stones stand in the woods with bewildering patterns on them hiding the one truth.Sanctum: Sword in the StoneRanka, a perfumer from Bloomville, asked you to find his partner: a rather dazed Emberpup. You’ve heard that Beast Fang Ridge is home to the Emberpup family. Could it be there? And besides being "dazed," what else might Ranka’s Emberpup partner be like?Give the Tanghulu to Jojo.Give <style=Hint_BgL>Vine Core</style> to RonTalk to the staff at ChillBeanz.View the Warehouse screen.You defeated Tucking. As it fled, a strange Hummin suddenly rushed out and stopped beside the pit, looking around. When you passed by, you heard it muttering to itself. Was that... the language of Idyllians?Deliver the Golden AnswerDriftwise Meadow: Not ActivatedThe Blazen is swift as lightning, with every strand of fur standing on end from the electricity coursing through its body.<BR>Respawn Interval: 20sContinue to craft the perfume with Sunia’s help.Marlowe loves using "strange" ingredients in his perfumes, and he wants your help finding one. But how do you define "strange"? <style=Hint_BgL>Berylline Vale</style>, famous for its unusual rocks, might be a good place to start.A painter is in trouble.Glow color (overrides basic color)Perfumer Marlowe likes to blend Perfume with “strange” Spice and hopes you can help find some. What counts as “strange” enough Spice? Perhaps <style=Hint_BgL>Berylline Causeway</style>, famed for its “odd stones,” will yield some clues.Keep talking to Senior LoullaDefeat the mysterious figure. Complete 4 required quests in Chapter 6.Elven EarsSanctum: Flaming WingsLook for the Nimbi at ChillBeanz.Explore Tideblossom Coast at night and learn about the legend of the Golden Shooting Star.What awaits me within the storm?With the Shellies’ last guardian gone, a group of Susuta has marched straight into Sherro territory. What are they really after?Lumin Amber: Floral MomentClue: Mysterious Presence: The Anomaly at Super ClawTwine with a Fentuft-family Aniimo.Inner Eye CornersHipsUpper Eyelid AngleChinEye CornersPupil ScaleNose TipNasal Root DepthEyeballsIris HighlightEyelidsCheeksUpper Eyelid FoldForearmsPupil Rotation SpeedLegsLower LipMor—phi!
